{
  "model": "437B",
  "manufacturer": "HP",
  "title": "HP 437B Power Meter",
  "manual": "437B-UM.pdf: Operating Manual, 437B Power Meter, 00437-90047 (Jan 1997), Section 4 Performance Tests (the Service Manual 00437-90016 has none)",
  "busDriver": "437B",
  "defaultResource": "GPIB0::13::INSTR",
  "channels": [
    "A"
  ],
  "warmupMinutes": 30,
  "notes": [
    "Over HP-IB the app presets (PR) and sets watts (LN), the range (RMnEN, or RA), the filter (FA) and cal factor 100% (KB100EN); zeroes with CSZE and calibrates on the 11683A with CSCL100EN, watching the status byte's Cal/Zero Complete bit (pp. 3-46 to 3-50, 3-106 to 3-108); and reads with TR2 (one settled reading), then TR3 (free run).",
    "Half-hour warm-up (p. 4-1). Perform the tests in the order given; record on Table 4-1 (p. 4-12)."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "zero-carryover",
      "title": "Zero Carryover Test",
      "source": "437B-UM.pdf, para 4-7, pp. 4-3 to 4-4 (PDF pp. 141-142); Table 4-1 p. 4-12 (PDF p. 150)",
      "reading": "Meter",
      "equipment": [
        "HP 11683A Range Calibrator",
        "HP 11730A power sensor cable"
      ],
      "setup": [
        "Connect the 11683A to the 437B with the 11730A cable (Figure 4-1). 437B LINE ON, PRESET/LOCAL then ENTER, dBm/W for watts.",
        "11683A: RANGE 3 µW, FUNCTION STANDBY, LINE ON.",
        "Press ZERO and wait about 15 s for ZEROING to clear; the display should read 0.00 ±0.06 µW.",
        "For each row press SET RANGE, choose RNG n with the arrow keys and press ENTER."
      ],
      "meter": {
        "display": "Watts",
        "filter": 0
      },
      "zero": {
        "calibrator": {
          "range": "3uW",
          "function": "Standby",
          "polarity": "Normal"
        },
        "settleSeconds": 60
      },
      "points": [
        {
          "label": "RNG 1",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "SET RANGE: RNG 1",
          "meter": {
            "range": 1
          },
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "uW",
          "min": -0.05,
          "max": 0.05
        },
        {
          "label": "RNG 2",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "SET RANGE: RNG 2",
          "meter": {
            "range": 2
          },
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "uW",
          "min": -0.1,
          "max": 0.1
        },
        {
          "label": "RNG 3",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "SET RANGE: RNG 3",
          "meter": {
            "range": 3
          },
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "mW",
          "min": -0.001,
          "max": 0.001
        },
        {
          "label": "RNG 4",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "SET RANGE: RNG 4",
          "meter": {
            "range": 4
          },
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "mW",
          "min": -0.01,
          "max": 0.01
        },
        {
          "label": "RNG 5",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "SET RANGE: RNG 5",
          "meter": {
            "range": 5
          },
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "mW",
          "min": -0.1,
          "max": 0.1
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Spec: ±0.5% of full scale on the most sensitive range, a tenth of that on each higher range, ±1 count. Drift and noise are included."
      ]
